Starter code:

class Solution:
    def maximizeSumOfWeights(self, edges: List[List[int]], k: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Following the process: this is a tree DP. Each node may keep at most k incident edges. Root the tree at 0; for each node v, let dp0[v] = best sum in v's subtree when v keeps at most k child edges (edge to parent not kept), and dp1[v] = best when v keeps at most k−1 child edges (edge to parent kept, so one slot is used by the parent edge).

For each child c with edge weight w: base = dp0[c] (edge not kept), gain = dp1[c] + w − dp0[c] (edge kept, child uses ≤k−1 of its own). Sort gains descending; dp0[v] = sum of base over children + sum of top k positive gains; dp1[v] = same but top k−1 positive gains.

Hand check on example 1: tree 0–1(4), 0–2(2), 2–3(12), 2–4(6), k=2. Leaves 1,3,4: dp0=0, dp1=0. Node 2: children 3 (w12), 4 (w6), gains 12 and 6 positive; dp0 = top 2 = 18 and dp1 = top 1 = 12. Node 0 with children 1 (w4), 2 (w2): gain of child 2 via kept edge = dp1[2] + 2 − dp0[2] = 12+2−18 = −4 (not positive), gain of child 1 = 0+4−0 = 4. dp0[0] = base sums (dp0[1]+dp0[2] = 18) + top 2 positive gains (only 4) = 22 ✓.

Complexity: sort per node, total O(n log n). I'll use an iterative DFS to avoid recursion limits.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "T-2737", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def maximizeSumOfWeights(self, edges: List[List[int]], k: int) -> int:\n        n = len(edges) + 1\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        for u, v, w in edges:\n            adj[u].append((v, w))\n            adj[v].append((u, w))\n\n        parent = [-1] * n\n        pw = [0] * n\n        order = []\n        visited = [False] * n\n        stack = [0]\n        visited[0] = True\n        while stack:\n            v = stack.pop()\n            order.append(v)\n            for to, w in adj[v]:\n                if not visited[to]:\n                    visited[to] = True\n                    parent[to] = v\n                    pw[to] = w\n                    stack.append(to)\n\n        dp0 = [0] * n  # node keeps at most k child edges\n        dp1 = [0] * n  # node keeps at most k-1 child edges (parent edge kept)\n\n        for v in reversed(order):\n            base = 0\n            gains = []\n            for to, w in adj[v]:\n                if to == parent[v]:\n                    continue\n                base += dp0[to]\n                g = dp1[to] + w - dp0[to]\n                if g > 0:\n                    gains.append(g)\n            gains.sort(reverse=True)\n            dp0[v] = base + sum(gains[:k])\n            dp1[v] = base + sum(gains[:k - 1]) if k - 1 > 0 else base\n\n        return dp0[0]\n"}

