Starter code:

class Solution:
    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Derivation first. The pattern splits into three fixed pieces: A (before the first '*'), B (between the stars), C (after the second '*'). A matching substring is A, then some gap, then B, then some gap, then C, with the gaps arbitrary. To minimize length, I want the earliest-possible placement at each step, which is a greedy chain of occurrences: pick the first occurrence of A starting at position ≥ 0 at start a; then the first occurrence of B starting at ≥ a+|A|; then the first occurrence of C starting at ≥ b+|B|. The substring spans from a to end of C.

But the shortest is not necessarily the greedy one from a single start, so I must try every start occurrence of A. For each occurrence a of A (in order), greedily find the first B at or after a+|A| and then the first C at or after that B's end. The length is end_C − a. Taking the minimum over all starts a gives the answer. Using occurrence lists plus binary search, each query is O(log n), giving O(n log n) total.

Edge cases: if A or C is empty, the empty piece matches at the current position with zero length, which the same procedure handles (the empty pattern occurs at every index). If a piece is empty, I treat its occurrences as all positions 0..n.

Hand check example 4: s="madlogic", p="*adlogi*". A empty, B="adlogi", C empty. First B occurrence at index 1 (ends at 7), so length 6 ✓.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "T-5301", "code": "import bisect\n\nclass Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        n = len(s)\n        i1 = p.index('*')\n        i2 = p.index('*', i1 + 1)\n        A = p[:i1]\n        B = p[i1 + 1:i2]\n        C = p[i2 + 1:]\n\n        def occurrences(pat):\n            # all start positions where pat occurs in s (empty pattern: all positions 0..n)\n            if pat == \"\":\n                return list(range(n + 1))\n            res = []\n            start = s.find(pat)\n            while start != -1:\n                res.append(start)\n                start = s.find(pat, start + 1)\n            return res\n\n        occA = occurrences(A)\n        occB = occurrences(B)\n        occC = occurrences(C)\n        if not occA or not occB or not occC:\n            return -1\n\n        best = None\n        for a in occA:\n            # first B starting at or after a + |A|\n            j = bisect.bisect_left(occB, a + len(A))\n            if j == len(occB):\n                continue\n            b = occB[j]\n            # first C starting at or after b + |B|\n            k = bisect.bisect_left(occC, b + len(B))\n            if k == len(occC):\n                continue\n            c = occC[k]\n            end = c + len(C)\n            length = end - a\n            if best is None or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best if best is not None else -1\n"}

