To keep it efficient, I compute for each `i` the best prefix value `best[i] = min over j<=i of dp[j]` in terms of a "run ended at j with any letter", and only allow the transition to start a new run at a different letter. Tie-breaking by lexicographic order is handled by comparing candidate strings, which is acceptable given n <= 5*10^4 with only 26 letters if I keep per-position best strings compactly as (cost, letter-run-sequence) pointers rather than full strings; reconstruct the answer at the end.

