1 <= l <= r < 10^9

Starter code:

class Solution:
    def beautifulNumbers(self, l: int, r: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a digit DP. For a bound N, count beautiful numbers in [1, N] by tracking: position, tight flag, started flag, digit sum (up to 81), and product of digits (the product is at most 9^9, but the number of distinct products of digits is small — only products of form 2^a·3^b·5^c·7^d, so I memoize on the product value directly).

The answer is count(r) - count(l-1). A number is beautiful when `product % sum == 0`, with the number itself positive (so 0 is excluded).

