class Solution:
    def minimumIncrements(self, nums: List[int], target: List[int]) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a bitmask DP over the targets (at most 4, so 16 masks). Let `dp[mask]` be the minimum operations so that the targets in `mask` are covered. Each element of `nums` can be incremented to some value `v >= nums[i]`, and it covers a subset of targets if `v` is a multiple of their LCM (or each target individually). Since the number of targets is tiny, for each subset `S` I compute `lcm(S)` and the cost to raise one element to the nearest multiple of that lcm: `ceil(x / L) * L - x`. The problem reduces to assigning distinct elements to disjoint target subsets, which I handle with DP over elements and masks.

Implementation: `dp[mask]` = min cost covering exactly `mask` using processed elements, with each element used at most once. For each element, I update masks from a snapshot so each element contributes to at most one subset.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-4021", "code": "from typing import List\nfrom math import gcd\n\nclass Solution:\n    def minimumIncrements(self, nums: List[int], target: List[int]) -> int:\n        t = len(target)\n        full = (1 << t) - 1\n        INF = float('inf')\n\n        # lcm for each subset of targets\n        lcm_of = [1] * (1 << t)\n        for mask in range(1, 1 << t):\n            low = mask & (-mask)\n            idx = low.bit_length() - 1\n            prev = mask ^ low\n            a = lcm_of[prev]\n            b = target[idx]\n            lcm_of[mask] = a * b // gcd(a, b)\n\n        # cost[i][mask]: cost to raise nums[i] to a multiple of lcm_of[mask]\n        # Only subsets with lcm <= something reasonable matter; keep all.\n        dp = [INF] * (1 << t)\n        dp[0] = 0\n        # Each element can be assigned to at most one nonempty subset of targets.\n        # Limit to first t elements is not valid in general; but we allow all elements.\n        for x in nums:\n            ndp = dp[:]  # element unused\n            for mask in range(1, 1 << t):\n                L = lcm_of[mask]\n                c = (-(-x // L)) * L - x  # ceil(x/L)*L - x\n                for prev in range(1 << t):\n                    if dp[prev] == INF:\n                        continue\n                    if prev & mask:\n                        continue\n                    nm = prev | mask\n                    v = dp[prev] + c\n                    if v < ndp[nm]:\n                        ndp[nm] = v\n            dp = ndp\n        return dp[full]\n"}

