**Approach:** Let `cost[i]` = minimum operations to make the window `nums[i..i+x-1]` all equal. The optimal common value is the median of the window, so `cost[i]` = sum of |nums[j] - median| over the window. I maintain this with a sliding window using two multisets (a lower half and an upper half) tracking sums, which gives O(n log x) overall.

Then DP: `dp[j][p]` = min cost to pick `j` non-overlapping windows within the prefix ending at `p`. Transition: either skip index `p`, or take a window ending at `p` (starting at `p-x+1`) and add to `dp[j-1][p-x]`. Using `k ≤ 15` keeps this at O(n·k).

