Starter code:

class Solution:
    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Approach: split `p` by `*` into three parts: `pre`, `mid`, `suf` (any may be empty). A substring matches iff it starts with `pre`, contains `mid` after that, and ends with `suf` after that. For the shortest match, for each occurrence of `mid` at position `j` in `s`, we want the nearest occurrence of `pre` ending at or before `j` (the latest start position `i` with `s[i:i+len(pre)] == pre` and `i + len(pre) <= j`), and the nearest occurrence of `suf` starting at or after `j + len(mid)`. The length is then `(k + len(suf)) - i`, where `k` is that suffix's start.

I'll find all occurrences of each part with KMP-like matching (via `str.find` loops), then combine with two pointers.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-5301", "code": "class Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        first = p.index('*')\n        second = p.index('*', first + 1)\n        pre = p[:first]\n        mid = p[first + 1:second]\n        suf = p[second + 1:]\n        n = len(s)\n\n        def occurrences(pat):\n            res = []\n            if pat == \"\":\n                return list(range(n + 1))\n            start = 0\n            while True:\n                idx = s.find(pat, start)\n                if idx == -1:\n                    break\n                res.append(idx)\n                start = idx + 1\n            return res\n\n        pre_occ = occurrences(pre)\n        mid_occ = occurrences(mid)\n        suf_occ = occurrences(suf)\n        if not mid_occ or not pre_occ or not suf_occ:\n            return -1\n\n        lp, lm, ls = len(pre), len(mid), len(suf)\n        best = -1\n        import bisect\n        for j in mid_occ:\n            # latest prefix start i with i + lp <= j\n            pi = bisect.bisect_right(pre_occ, j - lp) - 1\n            if pi < 0:\n                continue\n            i = pre_occ[pi]\n            # earliest suffix start k >= j + lm\n            si = bisect.bisect_left(suf_occ, j + lm)\n            if si >= len(suf_occ):\n                continue\n            k = suf_occ[si]\n            length = (k + ls) - i\n            if best == -1 or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best\n"}

