Starter code:

class Solution:
    def minTimeToReach(self, moveTime: List[List[int]]) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a shortest-path problem where each room can only be entered at or after moveTime[i][j]. Dijkstra works: dist[cell] is the earliest arrival time. Moving from u to v takes one second, so the arrival time at v is max(dist[u], moveTime[v]) + 1. Waiting is allowed, so this is the right transition.

Checking example 1: [[0,4],[4,4]]. From (0,0) at t=0, enter (0,1): max(0,4)+1 = 5. Enter (1,0): max(0,4)+1 = 5. From (1,0) at 5 to (1,1): max(5,4)+1 = 6 ✓.

Checking example 3: [[0,1],[1,2]]. (0,1): max(0,1)+1 = 2. (1,0): max(0,1)+1 = 2. (1,1) from (0,1): max(2,2)+1 = 3 ✓.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-4953", "code": "import heapq\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def minTimeToReach(self, moveTime: List[List[int]]) -> int:\n        n = len(moveTime)\n        m = len(moveTime[0])\n        INF = float('inf')\n        dist = [[INF] * m for _ in range(n)]\n        dist[0][0] = 0\n        heap = [(0, 0, 0)]\n        while heap:\n            d, i, j = heapq.heappop(heap)\n            if d > dist[i][j]:\n                continue\n            if i == n - 1 and j == m - 1:\n                return d\n            for di, dj in ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)):\n                ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                if 0 <= ni < n and 0 <= nj < m:\n                    nd = max(d, moveTime[ni][nj]) + 1\n                    if nd < dist[ni][nj]:\n                        dist[ni][nj] = nd\n                        heapq.heappush(heap, (nd, ni, nj))\n        return dist[n - 1][m - 1]\n"}

