class Solution:
    def minCost(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This ticket is a DP. The state is the remaining array, but at each step only the first three elements matter, and the removal picks two of them. The array shrinks from the front, so I can index by the current start position and track which of the next up-to-two elements remain. Since removing from the first three can leave an arbitrary subset of those three, the state is (start index, a bitmask of which of the next two elements are still present). A simpler, equivalent formulation: define dp over the suffix starting at i, where the first three of the current array are the element at i plus a subset of i+1..i+2 remaining. I'll use memoization on the tuple of the current first up-to-three elements, with the remainder tracked by index.

Checking example 1: [6,2,8,4]. Pair (6,8) cost 8, then remaining [2,4] costs 4 → 12 ✓. Example 2: [2,1,3,3]: pair (2,1) cost 2, remaining [3,3] costs 3 → 5 ✓.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-1052", "code": "from typing import List\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\nclass Solution:\n    def minCost(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        n = len(nums)\n\n        @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n        def solve(i, window):\n            # window: tuple of remaining elements from the current array's front (values),\n            # with the rest of the array being nums[i:]\n            rest_start = i\n            cur = list(window)\n            # pull elements from nums to keep window size up to 3\n            while len(cur) < 3 and rest_start < n:\n                cur.append(nums[rest_start])\n                rest_start += 1\n            if not cur:\n                return 0\n            if len(cur) < 3:\n                return max(cur)\n            best = float('inf')\n            # choose any two of the first three to remove\n            for a in range(3):\n                for b in range(a + 1, 3):\n                    cost = max(cur[a], cur[b])\n                    leftover = tuple(cur[c] for c in range(3) if c != a and c != b)\n                    best = min(best, cost + solve(rest_start, leftover))\n            return best\n\n        return solve(0, ())\n"}

