class Solution:
    def findMaxSum(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:


=== MODEL ===
Approach: sort indices by nums1. Process groups of equal nums1 values in increasing order. For each group, the answer is the sum of the top-k nums2 values among all strictly smaller nums1 elements inserted so far. Maintain a min-heap of size k holding the k largest values seen so far, plus a running sum. Then for each element in the group, answer = current heap sum; after computing answers for the whole group, insert the group's elements into the heap.

Checking Example 1: nums1=[4,2,1,5,3], nums2=[10,20,30,40,50], k=2. Sorted by nums1: (1,30),(2,20),(3,50),(4,10),(5,40). Before inserting 1: sum 0 → ans[2]=0. Before 2: heap {30}, sum 30 → ans[1]=30. Before 3: heap {30,20}, sum 50 → ans[4]=50. Before 4: heap {50,30}, sum 80 → ans[0]=80. Before 5: heap {50,30}, sum 80 → ans[3]=80. Matches [80,30,0,80,50].

This runs in O(n log k).
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-8777", "code": "from typing import List\nimport heapq\n\nclass Solution:\n    def findMaxSum(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:\n        n = len(nums1)\n        order = sorted(range(n), key=lambda i: nums1[i])\n        ans = [0] * n\n        heap = []  # min-heap of the up-to-k largest nums2 values seen so far\n        total = 0\n        i = 0\n        while i < n:\n            j = i\n            # group of equal nums1 values\n            while j < n and nums1[order[j]] == nums1[order[i]]:\n                j += 1\n            # answers for this group use only strictly smaller nums1 values\n            for t in range(i, j):\n                ans[order[t]] = total\n            # insert group's values into the heap\n            for t in range(i, j):\n                v = nums2[order[t]]\n                if len(heap) < k:\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, v)\n                    total += v\n                elif v > heap[0]:\n                    total += v - heapq.heapreplace(heap, v)\n            i = j\n        return ans\n"}

