Starter code:

class Solution:
    def maxSum(self, grid: List[List[int]], limits: List[int], k: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
The approach: from each row, the best choices are its largest elements, so sort each row descending and take the top limits[i] values. Gather all those candidate values into one pool, sort descending, and take the top k. Since within a row we only take a prefix of the sorted row, and the global greedy picks largest values first, the per-row limit is respected automatically as long as we only take up to limits[i] from each row's sorted list.

